1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,004
Valet demo: A fresh macOS machine. Everything in this run is fake: a made-up shop, a test account and a scripted chat.

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:10,601
1 · Install: Open the downloaded disk image, as a new user would

3
00:00:10,601 --> 00:00:16,890
1 · Install: Copy Valet Demo into Applications (the script copies it; a person drags the icon)

4
00:00:16,890 --> 00:00:19,894
1 · Install: Installed. This test build is unsigned and was never downloaded, so Gatekeeper does not ask about it

5
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:26,304
2 · Set up: First launch. (Started with a debugging port that only this demo build accepts, so the script can drive it)

6
00:00:26,304 --> 00:00:30,023
2 · Set up: Valet opens its first-run setup

7
00:00:30,023 --> 00:00:34,096
2 · Set up: Where logins come from. In the demo, a test provider stands in for 1Password

8
00:00:34,096 --> 00:00:42,770
2 · Set up: Review the shop adapter: the sites it may reach, and what each tool can do

9
00:00:42,770 --> 00:00:43,830
2 · Set up: Approve it. Until now its tools were hidden from every chat client

10
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:54,964
2 · Set up: Let the adapter use the login, typed only into the shop’s sign-in page

11
00:00:54,964 --> 00:01:02,744
2 · Set up: The shop texts a code at sign-in, so let Valet read that one sender’s codes (here from the fake’s outbox, not Messages)

12
00:01:02,744 --> 00:01:14,520
2 · Set up: Prices and stock follow a store, so pick the pick-up store the tools shop at

13
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:26,871
2 · Set up: Connect a chat app. Valet gives it a config that starts its own bridge, with no token in it

14
00:01:26,871 --> 00:01:37,991
3 · Chat: Now a chat app. This one is a scripted stand-in for Claude that speaks real MCP

15
00:01:37,991 --> 00:01:46,796
3 · Chat: Paste the config Valet copied

16
00:01:46,796 --> 00:01:59,322
3 · Chat: Connected through Valet’s bridge: 6 tools

17
00:01:59,322 --> 00:03:00,157
3 · Chat: The agent searches the shop through Valet. Searching needs no login

18
00:03:00,157 --> 00:03:19,120
3 · Chat: Valet spaces the shop’s requests 10 to 15 seconds apart, so this is unhurried on purpose

19
00:03:19,120 --> 00:04:19,270
Valet answers at once that it is logging in, and the agent calls again when told

20
00:04:19,270 --> 00:04:59,373
Valet: an earlier call still holds the shop's turn. Call again in 10 s.

21
00:04:59,373 --> 00:06:41,507
Valet: an earlier call still holds the shop's turn. Call again in 10 s.

22
00:06:41,507 --> 00:07:18,178
3 · Chat: The agent reads the trolley back

23
00:07:18,178 --> 00:07:27,416
4 · Valet: Back in Valet: every call, and the login, is in its audited activity log

24
00:07:27,416 --> 00:07:34,875
5 · Checkout: Now the shopper opens the shop’s website to check out

25
00:07:34,875 --> 00:07:42,805
5 · Checkout: Sign in on the shop’s own login page (a stand-in for its Auth0 page), with the test account

26
00:07:42,805 --> 00:07:51,750
5 · Checkout: The shop texts a code. A test phone page shows it

27
00:07:51,750 --> 00:07:58,031
5 · Checkout: The trolley holds what the agent added through Valet

28
00:07:58,031 --> 00:08:03,599
5 · Checkout: Checkout: pick up today. The person places the order; Valet’s MVP never does

29
00:08:03,599 --> 00:08:08,711
5 · Checkout: Order 100000001 placed

30
00:08:08,711 --> 00:08:28,691
6 · Done: Back in the chat, the agent can see the trolley is empty now

31
00:08:28,691 --> 00:08:32,898
Valet demo: End of the demo
